    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0562" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1765</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-08T13:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1918, 1
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 9, 8.46 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>492. From source considered reliable it is learned that Count Mirbach<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d580-f1"/> has presented an ultimatum to the Soviet
                    authorities stating that if British and French troops do not at once evacuate
                    Murman Peninsula the consequence will be most grave and it will be necessary for
                    Germany to undertake military operations occupying further territory either in
                    the direction of Murmansk or elsewhere.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d580-f1" n="3" xml:id="d580-f1-content">
                <p>Wilhelm, Count von Mirbach, German Ambassador to the Russian Socialist Federated
                    Soviet Republic.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
